PATCH 477: the AH-64 turret slew 90db/90cd -- it fed the aiming solver a265 a HOST pointer where a265
takes a DGROUP NEAR offset, so a265's result stores went through the pointer's low 16 bits and overwrote
the frame loop's own service vector at DGROUP:0x6ce4.

902c (patch 365) holds the object as a host pointer and passes it down to 90cd->90db, but a265 (patch 274)
takes DI as a near offset -- it did `(uint16_t)param_3` on a host address, landing its word[di+0x38] /
[di+0x99] / [di+0x9b] stores on DGROUP:0x6ce3..0x6ce6.  In the AZER1 self-play that clobbered word[0x6ce4]
(the per-frame service vector 459a calls at asm 0x45ed, legitimately 0xc30e/0x5db8/0x773e) with 0x000e, so
459a dispatched into FUN_0000_4700 with a garbage DI and SEGV'd -- a corruption whose crash site was three
subsystems away from its cause (found with a value-filtered hardware watchpoint on the vector).
Also rebuilt both functions at the asm's WORD widths ([di+0x10]/[di+0x26]/[di+0x89]/[di+0x8b]/[di+0x97]/
[di+0x9b] are all 16-bit; Ghidra's 32-bit `int` accesses clobbered each neighbouring field).
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -24239,8 +24239,13 @@
 void __allregs FUN_0000_90cd(undefined2 param_1,undefined4 param_2,int param_3)
 
 {
+  /* PATCH 477: asm 0x90cd-0x90da -- `call 90db; mov ax,[di+0x26]; add ax,[di+0x89]; mov [di+0x10],ax`.
+   * All three fields are WORDs; Ghidra read/wrote them as 32-bit `int` (so [di+0x10] clobbered
+   * [di+0x12] and the sum came from the wrong bytes).  param_3 = the object HOST pointer (902c's
+   * convention, patch 365). */
+  unsigned char *o = (unsigned char *)(intptr_t)param_3;
   FUN_0000_90db(param_1,param_2,param_3);
-  *(int *)(param_3 + 0x10) = *(int *)(param_3 + 0x26) + *(int *)(param_3 + 0x89);
+  *(uint16_t *)(o + 0x10) = (uint16_t)(*(uint16_t *)(o + 0x26) + *(uint16_t *)(o + 0x89));
   return;
 }
 
@@ -24250,26 +24255,39 @@
